What:		/dev/s3mX
Date:		Oct 2024
KernelVersion:	6.6
Contact:	"Will Skrydlak" <will.j.skrydlak@linux.intel.com>
Description:
		This interface provides issuance of commands to the S3M (Secure
		Startup Services Module). Commands are relayed through the
		OOBMSM mailbox, and processed by the S3M. The S3M will return a
		response upon completion of command execution.

		The ABI is defined in [/include/uapi/]<linux/s3m_if.h>. The user
		must allocate a payload buffer to hold the request data and the
		response data. The response size must be greater than or equal
		to the request size. The payload allocation must be equal to
		response size.

		After sending the request payload to the S3M, the driver will
		wait until the OOBMSM sets the OBJECT_RDY flag or times out.
		Once the OBJECT_READY flag is set, the driver will read back the
		response data. If the response data size (determined by the
		driver) is larger than the payload allocation, an error will be
		returned. Otherwise, the response size will be updated, and the
		data will be copied back to the payload buffer.

		If malformed payloads are sent to the S3M, the driver may not
		produce an error. However, the S3M mailbox state machine may be
		in error. If that is the case, the next command sent to the
		driver, will attempt to reset the S3M by setting the ABORT bit.
		This should reset the S3M mailbox state.

		==========	=====
		Error Code	Cause
		==========	=====
		EIO		General mailbox failure.
		ETIMEDOUT	Timed out waiting for mailbox state change.
		ENOMEM		Failed to allocate memory.
		EAGAIN		Mailbox was in error state. Abort flag has been
				set. Mailbox reset has been triggered. Try
				sending command again.
		EINVAL		Request size was too large.
		EMSGSIZE	Response message was too long.
		ENODATA		Failed to get device data.
		EOPNOTSUPP	Invalid IOCTL command.
		EOVERFLOW	Addition of two values overflowed.
		EBADMSG		Mailbox discovery failed during probe
